{
  "info": {
    "name": "MedData Escrow API",
    "description": "Generated from openapi/openapi.yaml (v0.2.0) by `npm run postman:gen`. Do not edit by hand.\n\nMedData Escrow lets a researcher describe a study in plain English, match it\nto vendor datasets, and buy access through an **escrow** built on PayPal\nauthorize-then-capture. Funds are held (authorized) while the data is\ndelivered, captured once the buyer accepts it, and paid out to the vendor.\nA buyer can dispute while funds are held, and an operator resolves the\ndispute toward capture or void.\n\nAfter delivery the researcher asks plain-English questions. Each question is\nscreened for identifiers, compiled to aggregate-only SQL, re-checked, run\nvendor-side, put through small-cell suppression, and billed per answer at a\nserver-set fee.\n\n**All data is synthetic** (Synthea-generated cohorts). No real patient data\nis stored or returned.\n\nThe server, not the client, decides who pays what and who sees what:\nthe escrowed amount is always the dataset's listed price, queries require a\npaid and delivered order, and the per-query fee is fixed server-side.\n\nErrors are always `{ \"error\": string }`, plus `reasons: string[]` on\nprivacy rejections.\n\nRun with `PAYPAL_MODE=mock` to drive the whole escrow arc with no PayPal\ncredentials; responses then carry `mock: true` and `MOCK-*` ids.\n\nOperations marked `x-status: preview` are documented ahead of their\nimplementation landing and may change.\n",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Demo: full escrow arc",
      "description": "Run in order against a `PAYPAL_MODE=mock` server (`npm run dev:mock`). Matches a study, escrows the top dataset at its listed price, walks authorize → deliver → query → billing → capture → payout, and reads the audit trail. datasetId and orderId chain through collection variables.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1. Match a study to datasets",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"status is 200\", function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "const matches = pm.response.json().matches;",
                  "pm.test(\"returns at least one match\", function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(matches.length).to.be.above(0);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"datasetId\", matches[0].datasetId);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/match",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "match"]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"description\": \"Heart disease cohort with cardiology encounters\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
